<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<lint>
    <!--
      WearPasswordInput fires on anything that looks like a password field on a
      wrist. This app's password entry is a RemoteInput handoff: the watch asks,
      the phone's keyboard answers, so nothing is typed on the watch itself.

      On-watch email/password is a deliberate product decision, recorded in
      AGENTS.md under the :wear block — the watch must be able to sign in
      standalone when the phone is not around, not only through the Credential
      Manager sync path. Removing the field would trade a real offline
      capability for a lint rule aimed at a different interaction.

      Revisit only if the password entry stops being a RemoteInput handoff.
    -->
    <issue id="WearPasswordInput" severity="ignore" />
</lint>
